WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.589
We will start with the result shape of the inner
query Then we will learn

00:00:05.615 --> 00:00:11.260
scalar subqueries followed by set-oriented patterns
such as IN EXISTS ANY and ALL

00:00:13.003 --> 00:00:18.068
After that we will study correlated subqueries where
the inner query depends on the current

00:00:18.095 --> 00:00:25.385
outer row Finally we will compare placements and
rewrites This

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:30.358
order makes subqueries easier to understand because
every new pattern answers a specific kind of

00:00:30.385 --> 00:00:30.924
question
